From: GameShellNeo maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: retire the gadget session on system-sleep detach

Drain the controller IRQ after masking it, then notify a logical disconnect
for the session intentionally detached by fixed-peripheral system PM with
wakeup disabled. Retire before context save so cleanup runs while powered.
Keep pull-up intent for resume and suppress duplicate disconnect callbacks
once negotiated speed has been cleared. Callback lifetime is protected by
the preceding UDC admission/drain patch.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_core.c b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_core.c
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_core.c
@@ -2823,6 +2823,9 @@
 	musb_gadget_suspend(musb);
 	musb_platform_disable(musb);
 	musb_disable_interrupts(musb);
+	/* No IRQ callback may overlap retirement of the detached session. */
+	if (musb->gadget_suspended)
+		synchronize_irq(musb->nIrq);
 
 	musb->flush_irq_work = true;
 	while (flush_delayed_work(&musb->irq_work))
@@ -2835,6 +2838,12 @@
 	WARN_ON(!list_empty(&musb->pending_list));
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&musb->lock, flags);
+
+	/* The pull-up is gone: retire protocol state before saving context.
+	 * No later cable edge or host reset is required to finish disconnect.
+	 */
+	if (musb->gadget_suspended && musb->g.speed != USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN)
+		musb_g_disconnect(musb);
 
 	if (is_host_active(musb)) {
 		/* we know all the children are suspended; sometimes
diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
@@ -2082,8 +2082,10 @@
 	/* don't draw vbus until new b-default session */
 	(void) musb_gadget_vbus_draw(&musb->g, 0);
 
+	/* Retire once, including an IRQ arriving after a system-PM detach. */
+	driver = musb->g.speed != USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN ?
+		 musb_gadget_get_driver(musb) : NULL;
 	musb->g.speed = USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN;
-	driver = musb_gadget_get_driver(musb);
 	if (driver) {
 		if (driver->disconnect) {
 			spin_unlock(&musb->lock);
